WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:06.460
Rian Johnson's deliciously twisted whodunnit
Knives Out is finally… well, out.

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:10.530
Even if you paid close attention all throughout
the hilarious caper, you may be left with

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:11.260
some questions.

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:14.760
We're here to lay out everything you need
to know about the ending, and what really

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:16.480
happened to Harlan Thrombey.

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:22.520
To understand the ending of Knives Out, it's
important to first understand each character

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:25.390
in the film's sprawling cast, and how they're
all connected to one another.

00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:30.270
At the top of the family tree is Harlan's
wizened mother, Greatana Wanetta, who doesn't

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:32.340
say much, but sees a lot.

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:35.780
Then there's Harlan, and his two surviving
children, Linda and Walt.

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:41.030
Walt ostensibly runs Harlan's publishing house,
while Linda is a "self-made" businesswoman

00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:42.880
who built her business from the ground up.

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:46.180
"I'm Walt Thrombey.

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:49.710
And if that name sounds familiar, it's probably
because you know my dad."

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:52.750
In reality, Harlan is still the one pulling
the strings at the publishing house, and Linda

00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:57.269
got her start with a handy million-dollar
start-up loan from her father — of course.

00:00:57.269 --> 00:01:02.460
Beyond them, there's Joni, an Instagram influencer
whose husband, Harlan's son, died 15 years

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:03.000
earlier.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:05.920
She's been living off of Harlan's generosity
ever since.

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:10.440
Linda is married to Richard, and they have
an adult son, Hugh, although the family calls

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:12.040
him by his middle name, Ransom.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:15.840
Walt is married to Donna, and they have a
teenage son, Jacob.

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:19.120
And Joni has a college-aged daughter, Meg,
from her marriage to Harlan's son.

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:24.130
Also in the Thrombey family's orbit are Harlan's
housekeeper, Fran, and his personal nurse,

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:27.500
Marta Cabera, who also became his close friend
and confidante.

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:31.440
Although the Thrombeys often say they consider
Marta "part of the family" — a claim that's

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:34.940
constantly undermined by their inability to
remember what country she's from — the only

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:38.360
one she's really close to, other than Harlan,
is Meg.

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:43.090
Harlan's housekeeper Fran discovers him dead
on the couch in his study, covered in blood

00:01:43.090 --> 00:01:46.340
from a knife wound to the neck, apparently
self-inflicted.

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:50.619
His family had all come into town for his
85th birthday party the night before, and

00:01:50.619 --> 00:01:55.390
they wind up sticking around for the funeral,
will reading, and police investigation.

00:01:55.390 --> 00:01:59.380
Although Lieutenant Elliott, the investigator
assigned to the case, believes Harlan clearly

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:02.720
killed himself, he still covers his bases
by questioning everyone.

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:07.700
Conversely, renowned private investigator
Benoit Blanc suspects foul play right from

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:08.280
the get-go.

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:13.100
"I suspect foul play.

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:15.120
I have eliminated no suspects."

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:18.360
Technically, Blanc turns out to be only partially
right.

00:02:18.580 --> 00:02:23.240
No one killed Harlan Thrombey; he really did
do the deed himself by slitting his own throat.

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:27.520
But the actual circumstances surrounding his
death were far more complicated than that.

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:33.060
Early on, we get Marta's version of the events
that led to Harlan's death, which caused her

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:33.880
to believe that she killed him.

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:38.580
After Harlan's birthday party, Marta accompanied
him up to his study, where they played their

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:42.800
nightly round of the board game Go — which
Marta always won — and she gave him his

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:43.680
evening medication.

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:48.260
Occasionally, Marta would follow up his daily
meds with three milligrams of morphine, which

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:52.040
Harlan referred to as "the good stuff," to
help with the pain he'd been suffering since

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:53.160
a recent surgery.

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:57.200
Since it was Harlan's birthday, Marta thought
he'd earned a dose of "the good stuff" to

00:02:57.200 --> 00:03:01.030
help him sleep, but when she went to pick
up the vial of morphine, she realized the

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:02.060
bottles had been switched.

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:05.460
She had already given Harlan 100 milligrams
— a lethal dose.

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:09.680
Marta searched for the antagonist that would
counteract the overdose, but it was missing.

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:13.920
She tried to call 911, but Harlan stopped
her, knowing the ambulance wouldn't arrive

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:18.040
in time, and not wanting Marta to face scrutiny
that would lead to her undocumented mother

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:19.040
being deported.

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:23.240
Instead, before the morphine kicked in, Harlan
walked Marta through an elaborate plan to

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:24.440
keep her above suspicion.

00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:29.200
While Marta's version of events was the truth,
it wasn't the whole truth.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:33.200
It turned out that Harlan's grandson, Ransom,
had switched out the morphine with Harlan's

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:38.060
other meds earlier in the evening, intending
for Marta to administer the overdose of morphine

00:03:38.060 --> 00:03:40.760
while thinking it was his regular medication.

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:45.550
However, Ransom failed to take into account
Marta's professional expertise and familiarity

00:03:45.550 --> 00:03:49.980
with Harlan's evening routine, not to mention
Harlan's own tendency to be a sore loser,

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:52.520
all of which caused his plan to go sideways.

00:03:52.940 --> 00:03:56.120
Earlier in the evening, after Marta had set
out all of Harlan's medication beside the

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:59.200
Go board, she beat Harlan at the game yet
again.

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:03.520
Harlan knew she could beat him nearly every
time, yet still was convinced each time they

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:05.600
played that this time, he'd finally win.

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:10.190
When Marta won, Harlan overturned the game
board, sending his medication tumbling onto

00:04:10.190 --> 00:04:11.730
the floor along with the Go pieces.

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:15.730
When Marta retrieved the vials from the floor,
she didn't even look at the labels, instead

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:18.780
relying on her familiarity with what the bottles'
contents looked like.

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:23.050
So when she gave Harlan 100 milligrams of
the drug in the bottle labeled "morphine,"

00:04:23.050 --> 00:04:27.250
she was actually giving him the correct medication
— which means that if he'd allowed her to

00:04:27.250 --> 00:04:31.320
call the ambulance like she'd wanted, instead
of taking matters into his own hands, he would've

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:31.960
been just fine.

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:37.120
After financially supporting his family for
years, Harlan had come to the conclusion that

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:40.490
their financial dependence on him wasn't doing
any of them any favors.

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:44.660
They'd all all grown accustomed to the indulgent
lifestyle that Harlan's wealth afforded them,

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:48.480
and had convinced themselves that they deserved
it, even though they'd done nothing to earn

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:49.060
it.

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:52.700
Hoping to motivate them all to go make something
of themselves Harlan had decided to cut off

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:57.080
their access to his fortune, instead naming
Marta as his sole beneficiary.

00:04:57.400 --> 00:05:01.570
When Harlan turns up dead, multiple characters
begin referring to something called the "Slayer

00:05:01.570 --> 00:05:06.360
Rule" as a way to circumvent Harlan's wishes
and allow his family to inherit his estate.

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:10.940
Despite its dramatic name, the slayer rule
is actually a real thing, stating that a killer

00:05:10.940 --> 00:05:12.720
cannot inherit the property of their victim.

00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:17.160
Harlan left his entire estate to Marta, but
if the family could prove that she killed

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:18.480
him, it would void his will.

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:19.780
"Did you just Google that?"

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:20.960
"I did just Google that."

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:24.360
What's more, the slayer rule applies to civil
law, not criminal law.

00:05:24.580 --> 00:05:28.400
This means that Marta wouldn't actually have
to be convicted of Harlan's death for the

00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:30.470
Thrombeys to gain access to Harlan's money.

00:05:30.470 --> 00:05:34.650
All Ransom has to do in order to reclaim his
inheritance is amass enough evidence against

00:05:34.650 --> 00:05:39.340
Marta to file a wrongful death claim — a
much lower bar to clear than having to convince

00:05:39.340 --> 00:05:40.480
a jury of her guilt.

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:46.690
The mystery of who hired Blanc simmers throughout
Knives Out, and not even Blanc himself knows

00:05:46.690 --> 00:05:49.060
who his employer is until the end of the film.

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:54.000
He was hired with nothing more than an envelope
full of cash and a newspaper clipping of Harlan's

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:56.300
death, which was enough to pique his interest.

00:05:56.300 --> 00:06:00.040
It seems strange that someone would hire a
private investigator to dig into Harlan's

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:04.460
death — especially since the only person
who seems to know the full circumstances around

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:08.560
Thrombey's death is Marta, who has a vested
interest in no one finding out the truth.

00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:10.700
"CSI: KFC?"

00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:19.840
It turns out that Ransom was the one who sent
Blanc the cash and the newspaper clipping,

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:23.680
hoping that he would discover that Marta had
given Harlan a lethal dose of morphine, which

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:26.940
would trigger the slayer rule and prevent
her from inheriting his estate.

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:30.400
But of course, things don't wind up going
according to Ransom's plan.

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:35.000
Ransom was the only family member to learn
what Harlan was planning for his estate.

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:39.920
And from his time as Harlan's research assistant,
he also knew about the slayer rule, which

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:41.220
led to him hatching his plan.

00:06:41.550 --> 00:06:45.180
If he could make a case for Marta having killed
Harlan, then she wouldn't be able to inherit,

00:06:45.180 --> 00:06:47.320
allowing him to get the money he felt he was
owed.

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:51.560
Ransom switched the medications in Marta's
medical bag and removed the antidote that

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:55.380
could counteract the morphine, thinking that
when Harlan died of an overdose, it would

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:56.800
obviously point to Marta.

00:06:57.240 --> 00:07:01.560
But when Harlan slit his throat, Ransom needed
someone to make a more thorough investigation,

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:03.000
which is why he hired Blanc.

00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:08.670
When he realized that Harlan didn't overdose
after all, Ransom changed tactics again, destroying

00:07:08.670 --> 00:07:13.300
the autopsy records and endearing himself
to Marta so that she'd give him "his share"

00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:13.860
of the money.

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:18.460
But then when Fran attempted to blackmail
him, Ransom changed his plan yet again, intending

00:07:18.460 --> 00:07:22.120
to kill Fran and frame Marta for her death
instead of Harlan's.

00:07:23.020 --> 00:07:27.340
Since the Thrombeys opted not to invite "the
help" to Harlan's funeral, Fran the housekeeper

00:07:27.350 --> 00:07:31.120
was still at home when Ransom sneaked into
the house to replace the medications he'd

00:07:31.120 --> 00:07:32.880
tampered with in Marta's medical bag.

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:37.400
Fran had never liked Ransom, and grew immediately
suspicious that he'd done something shady.

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:42.640
She contacted her cousin in the medical examiner's
office and got a copy of the toxicology report

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:47.169
from Harlan's autopsy, which she didn't know
how to interpret, but assumed it said something

00:07:47.169 --> 00:07:48.360
to incriminate Ransom.

00:07:48.630 --> 00:07:52.880
Fran made a copy of the report's header, storing
the original in the same clock where she hid

00:07:52.880 --> 00:07:57.640
her marijuana — the "stash" she sometimes
shared with Marta and Meg — and sent it

00:07:57.640 --> 00:08:01.800
to Ransom with the note, "I know what you
did," along with a meeting time and place,

00:08:01.800 --> 00:08:03.540
where she intended to confront him.

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:08.560
Ransom in turn sent the note along to Marta,
giving her a slightly later meeting time,

00:08:08.560 --> 00:08:12.040
intending for her to show up as Fran died,
so that Marta would get arrested for killing

00:08:12.040 --> 00:08:12.580
Fran.

00:08:12.700 --> 00:08:16.820
When Ransom met Fran, he attacked her and
injected her with morphine, leaving her for

00:08:16.820 --> 00:08:17.320
dead.

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:21.460
But she's still alive when Marta arrives,
and manages to gasp out that the toxicology

00:08:21.540 --> 00:08:24.420
report was with her stash, and that "Hugh
did this."

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:30.000
Despite confusing this statement for an accusatory
"You did this," Marta nevertheless tries to

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:33.260
save Fran by calling 911 and administering
CPR.

00:08:33.500 --> 00:08:37.280
Fran eventually dies in the hospital, leading
to Ransom being arrested for her death.

00:08:38.690 --> 00:08:43.120
Blanc can tell from the first instant he meets
Marta that she knows more about Harlan's death

00:08:43.130 --> 00:08:46.880
than she's letting on, due to a small spatter
of blood on her white shoes.

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:47.940
"None of them are murderers."

00:08:48.180 --> 00:08:49.180
"We'll find out."

00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:53.760
When Marta finally comes clean to Blanc after
trying to save Fran, he thinks he has all

00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:54.300
the pieces.

00:08:54.640 --> 00:08:58.380
But it isn't until he reads the toxicology
report that Blanc finally realizes what happened,

00:08:58.380 --> 00:08:59.700
and who is to blame.

00:09:00.180 --> 00:09:04.570
He realizes the second he looks at it that
Harlan hadn't suffered an overdose, that someone

00:09:04.570 --> 00:09:08.490
must have intentionally switched Harlan's
medications, and based on the events of the

00:09:08.490 --> 00:09:11.180
night of Harlan's party, he knows it must
have been Ransom.

00:09:11.640 --> 00:09:15.850
While his suspicions may not have been enough
to get Ransom convicted, it turns out that

00:09:15.850 --> 00:09:20.080
Marta tricked Ransom by telling him Fran was
alive, prompting Ransom to brag to Blanc that

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:21.600
he'd gotten away with everything.

00:09:22.140 --> 00:09:26.700
But unbeknownst to Ransom, Marta was lying,
and managed to hold off her regurgitation

00:09:26.700 --> 00:09:31.220
reflex just long enough for Trooper Wagner
to record Ransom's entire confession.

00:09:32.240 --> 00:09:36.620
After spending the entire film in a constant
state of panic, Marta is able to rest easy

00:09:36.620 --> 00:09:40.460
at the end, knowing that nothing she did led
to Harlan's death, and that she helped the

00:09:40.460 --> 00:09:44.120
police find the person truly responsible for
what happened to him.

00:09:44.620 --> 00:09:49.380
Marta's lack of culpability in Harlan's death
means that the Thrombey family has no grounds

00:09:49.390 --> 00:09:54.400
on which to contest Harlan's will, allowing
Marta to claim her entire inheritance, which

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:59.200
consists of the publishing house, the mansion,
the rights to all of Harlan's written works,

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:00.280
and $60 million.

00:10:01.180 --> 00:10:05.900
We last see her sipping from a mug that says
"My House, My Rules, My Coffee," first seen

00:10:05.900 --> 00:10:10.611
way back in the opening shot of the film,
standing over the rest of the Thrombey family

00:10:10.620 --> 00:10:11.520
on the mansion's balcony.

